  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GreenCAFS, water-efficient fire suppression for climate resilience in South Africa, Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GreenCAFS is a low-cost, water-efficient fire-suppression system for farmers and rural communities in Africa, where wildfires and farm fires routinely outpace distant municipal services. The 200-litre, low-pressure unit produces stable compressed-air foam that covers 20&#x2013;50&#xd7; more surface than water, cutting water use by up to 90% and enabling faster first-attack by the farmers themselves. Built from circular components (re-used truck air tanks) and biodegradable, plant-based surfactants from local soap-skim, GreenCAFS is inexpensive to build and simple to operate from the back of a pickup or quad. GreenCAFS empowers farmers and rural communities to contain fires faster, protecting their future.</narrative>
  </description>
